 144:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****     (+) PeriodElapsedHalfCpltCallback     : TIM Period Elapsed half complete Callback.
 145:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****     (+) TriggerCallback                   : TIM Trigger Callback.
 146:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****     (+) TriggerHalfCpltCallback           : TIM Trigger half complete Callback.
 147:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****     (+) IC_CaptureCallback                : TIM Input Capture Callback.
 148:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****     (+) IC_CaptureHalfCpltCallback        : TIM Input Capture half complete Callback.
 149:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****     (+) OC_DelayElapsedCallback           : TIM Output Compare Delay Elapsed Callback.
 150:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****     (+) PWM_PulseFinishedCallback         : TIM PWM Pulse Finished Callback.
 151:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****     (+) PWM_PulseFinishedHalfCpltCallback : TIM PWM Pulse Finished half complete Callback.
 152:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****     (+) ErrorCallback                     : TIM Error Callback.
 153:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****     (+) CommutationCallback               : TIM Commutation Callback.
 154:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****     (+) CommutationHalfCpltCallback       : TIM Commutation half complete Callback.
 155:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****     (+) BreakCallback                     : TIM Break Callback.
 156:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****     (+) Break2Callback                    : TIM Break2 Callback.
 157:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****     (+) EncoderIndexCallback              : TIM Encoder Index Callback.
 158:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****     (+) DirectionChangeCallback           : TIM Direction Change Callback
 159:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****     (+) IndexErrorCallback                : TIM Index Error Callback.
 160:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****     (+) TransitionErrorCallback           : TIM Transition Error Callback
 161:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c **** 
 162:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****   [..]
 163:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c **** By default, after the Init and when the state is HAL_TIM_STATE_RESET
 164:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c **** all interrupt callbacks are set to the corresponding weak functions:
 165:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****   examples HAL_TIM_TriggerCallback(), HAL_TIM_ErrorCallback().
 166:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c **** 
 167:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****   [..]
 168:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****   Exception done for MspInit and MspDeInit functions that are reset to the legacy weak
 169:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****   functionalities in the Init / DeInit only when these callbacks are null
 170:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****   (not registered beforehand). If not, MspInit or MspDeInit are not null, the Init / DeInit
 171:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****     keep and use the user MspInit / MspDeInit callbacks(registered beforehand)
 172:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c **** 
 173:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****   [..]
 174:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****     Callbacks can be registered / unregistered in HAL_TIM_STATE_READY state only.
 175:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****     Exception done MspInit / MspDeInit that can be registered / unregistered
 176:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****     in HAL_TIM_STATE_READY or HAL_TIM_STATE_RESET state,
 177:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****     thus registered(user) MspInit / DeInit callbacks can be used during the Init / DeInit.
 178:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****   In that case first register the MspInit/MspDeInit user callbacks
 179:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****       using HAL_TIM_RegisterCallback() before calling DeInit or Init function.
 180:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c **** 
 181:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****   [..]
 182:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****       When The compilation define USE_HAL_TIM_REGISTER_CALLBACKS is set to 0 or
 183:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****       not defined, the callback registration feature is not available and all callbacks
 184:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c ****       are set to the corresponding weak functions.
 185:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_tim.c **** 
